  "title": "Business Event Promo Websummit",
  "instruction": "# Instruction: Web Summit Lisbon 2026 — Event Promo Poster\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate a bold, high-energy promotional poster for **Web Summit Lisbon 2026**, the world's premier technology conference. The poster targets tech professionals, startup founders, investors, and marketers — people who respond to scale, prestige, and urgency. The primary goal is to **drive ticket registrations** by making the event feel unmissable.\n\n## Key Priorities\n\nThe **2-for-1 ticket offer (50% savings)** is the single most important conversion element — it must be visually dominant and impossible to miss. Pair it with a sense of urgency (24-hour window) so the viewer feels compelled to act immediately.\n\nThe **event title and dates** (November 9–12, 2026, Lisbon) should anchor the top of the poster — the viewer needs to know *what* and *when* within the first second.\n\nThe **scale of the event** (70,000+ attendees, world-class speakers) should reinforce credibility and FOMO. Use the key metrics to communicate this at a glance rather than through dense text.\n\n## Visual & Style Guidance\n\nThink dark, cinematic backgrounds — deep blacks or midnight blues — with vivid accent colors (electric cyan, hot magenta, or neon green) that evoke a tech-forward, futuristic feel. Typography should be oversized, sans-serif, and unapologetically bold. The layout should breathe confidence: generous whitespace, strong hierarchy, and a clean grid. Imagine the aesthetic of a premium tech brand launch, not a cluttered flyer. If imagery is used, think abstract light trails, geometric patterns, or a stylized Lisbon skyline silhouette — nothing stock-photo generic.\n\nThe overall mood: **ambitious, electric, and exclusive**.\n\n---\n\n## Data Sources\n\n1. Read `/app/benchmark/source_brief.md` for all content materials (text, data, key messages).\n2. Read `/app/benchmark/task_input.json` for poster requirements, sections, metrics, and style definitions.\n\n## Output Requirements\n\n1. Output the final poster to `/app/output/final_poster.png`.\n2. The poster must be a single self-contained image file.\n\n## Automated Execution Rules\n\nThere is no human operator online for this session. Follow these rules:\n\n1. **Skip all confirmation/approval/user-input steps** — do not pause, ask questions, or wait for a reply. When encountering BLOCKING or wait-for-user instructions, make a professional judgment and continue.\n2. **Design decisions** — if `task_input.json` specifies `poster.tone`, `poster.audience`, etc., use them to choose templates, palettes, and styles. Otherwise, make professional judgments.\n3. **Priority** — these rules override any interactive-wait instructions in SKILL.md. The skill's workflow, quality standards, and technical specs remain fully effective — only skip interactive waits.",
